---
title: Shop — built with Darkmown
description: A storefront in Markdown — live search, a shared cart, and a checkout that posts to a serverless function.
transitions: true
---

@include /nav.wd

<main>

::: section #shop

:store cart = []
:state q = ""
:computed itemCount = count(cart)
:computed subtotal = sum(cart, price)

# Shop

::: shop-search
:bind q placeholder="Search products…"
:::

::: catalog
@loop /products.json into p where p.name contains q
::: card .product
::: emoji
{ p.emoji }
:::
::: pname
{ p.name }
:::
::: price
{ p.price | money }
:::
:button "Add to cart" -> cart += p
:::
@empty
::: card .empty
Nothing matches "**{ q }**".
:::
@endloop
:::

## Your cart ({ itemCount })

@loop cart into item
::: card .line
{ item.emoji } **{ item.name }** — { item.price | money }
:button "Remove" -> cart remove item
:::
@empty
Your cart is empty — add something above.
@endloop

:if itemCount
::: cart-foot
**Subtotal: { subtotal | money }**
:::

### Checkout

This form posts to `api/checkout.js` — a plain serverless function that runs in
`darkmown dev` and on Vercel/Cloudflare alike. With JavaScript off it degrades to
a native POST.

:form action="/api/checkout" into receipt
:input name placeholder="Full name" required
:input email type=email placeholder="you@example.com" required
:submit "Place order"
:endform

:if receipt
::: card .receipt
**Order placed ✓** — thanks { receipt.received.name }. A confirmation is on its way
to { receipt.received.email }. Order { receipt.orderId }.
:::
:endif
:endif

:::

</main>
